  "summary": "Georgetown, Indiana police officer Justin Craig was arrested and charged with official misconduct and fraud after an internal review found he used Flock ALPR cameras over 300 times to search his wife's and her acquaintance's license plates, mislabeling the queries as legitimate investigations. The tip was triggered by a Washington Post reporter contacting the Georgetown police chief.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "he searched his wife's license plate more than 80 times and that of a \"previous acquaintance\" of hers nearly 250 times",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "An internal review by the Georgetown police found that the searches Craig conducted on the Flock system were unrelated to any police investigations, and he had intentionally mislabeled those searches to make them appear justified.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "The conduct alleged does not violate any law or department policy.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
